 "result": "All of it is in `src/tessel/views.py`, in two classes.\n\n**1. `View.to_view_func(name, ...)`** (L86, classmethod) turns the class into a view function:\n- It builds an inner `view(**kwargs)` function.\n  - By default (`init_every_request=True`) it creates a new instance of `view.view_class` on each request.\n  - If `init_every_request` is `False`, it reuses a single instance.\n  - Either way it calls `active_app.ensure_sync(self.run_view)(**kwargs)`.\n- It applies any `decorators` from the class.\n- It then attaches `view_class`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` to the function. These are what `attach_route_rule` reads when registering the route.\n\n**2. `VerbView`** (L138, extends `View`) routes each HTTP method to its handler:\n- `__init_subclass__` (L165) auto-fills `cls.methods`.\n  - It collects the uppercase names of any of `http_method_funcs` that the class defines, such as `get` and `post`.\n  - It also inherits `methods` from base classes.\n  - It skips this if the class sets `methods` itself.\n- `run_view` (L182) does the dispatch.\n  - It calls `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`.\n  - `HEAD` falls back to `get` if there is no `head` handler.\n  - An unimplemented method trips an assertion.\n  - The handler runs through `ensure_sync` with the URL variables as kwargs.",
